Christy,

A PCoA of the genomic data, using the appropriate distance measure, and then a PCA of shape (which uses Procrustes Distance) would mean that the resulting PC-coordinates from both are in similar units. Thus theoretically, they could then be combined into a global analysis.

The one bit that is somewhat data-dependent is the scale of the resulting PC-coordinates from both. They may be a bit wonky relative to one another, due to scaling of the original variables. Thus, inputs from standard normal deviates may also be required. This part requires a bit of exploration with your particular data.

Dean

